#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059563 :question/id #uuid "8cd94856-fbe5-53a4-b7f2-f5b29b7aa927" :question/math-academy-id "e-4514" :question/problem "Find the inverse of $A={\\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & - 3 & 8\\end{array} \\right]}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 8\\end{vmatrix} & =0\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{vmatrix}+2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =0-(8-12)+2(-3-0) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 8\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 14 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC={\\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc}9 & - ( - 4 ) & - 3 \\\\ - ( 14 ) & - 8 & - ( - 4 ) \\\\ 3 & - ( - 2 ) & - 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n={\\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc}9 & 4 & - 3 \\\\ - 14 & - 8 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 2 & - 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\nC^{T}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc}9 & - 14 & 3 \\\\ 4 & - 8 & 2 \\\\ - 3 & 4 & - 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -14 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -14 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -8 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{9}{2} & 7 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & -2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059564 :question/id #uuid "9180ff3b-46d2-5df7-81b6-ac75bef51e00" :question/math-academy-id "e-4515" :question/problem "The entry $a'_{31}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\nA={\\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc}3 & 2 & - 2 \\\\ - 2 & k & 0 \\\\ - 1 & - 3 & 3\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$ \nequals $1$. Find the value of $k$." :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & k & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & =3\\begin{vmatrix}k & 0 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & k \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(3k-0)-2(-6-0)-2(6+k) \\\\  & =9k+12-12-2k \\\\  & =7k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry $a'_{31}$ in $A^{-1},$ we need to know the value of $c_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & k \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & k \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =6+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since $A^{-1}=\\dfrac{1}{\\det (A)}C^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7k}\\cdot (6+k) \\\\  & =\\frac{6+k}{7k}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that $a'_{31}=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6+k}{7k} & =1 \\\\ 6+k & =7k \\\\ 6 & =6k \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059565 :question/id #uuid "26e9a55f-7711-5d8f-ab0a-e8638f2d2dec" :question/math-academy-id "e-4516" :question/problem "Determine the entry $a'_{23}$ in the inverse of the matrix $A={\\left[ \\begin{array}{ccc}- 2 & 3 & - 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & - 1 & 2\\end{array} \\right]}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =-2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-2(2-0)-3(0-0)-3(0-1) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry $a'_{23}$ in $A^{-1},$ we need to know the value of $c_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}{M}_{32} \\\\  & =(-1)^{5}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-1\\cdot (0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since $A^{-1}=\\dfrac{1}{\\det (A)}C^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\na'_{23} = \\dfrac{1}{-1}c_{32} = -1\\cdot 0 = 0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060153 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f06230e-8816-51ce-b392-2abd455f3b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285208} {:answer/id #uuid "4e8539bc-f4a1-50db-90f6-0b45e3ceff04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285517} {:answer/id #uuid "52f9a129-aa6f-59fe-9748-78c62d9d1a3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285550} {:answer/id #uuid "d79adfbb-4209-5e76-80b7-c3a2f369dbcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286751} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b8e647-e565-5c04-9e76-013451742246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287048}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285517} :answer-field/id #uuid "cec0d804-b8fa-5b33-8525-d5694c64c34d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ce77ea41-d1eb-55f8-914d-e1a94a42a6b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-18279" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+4\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(6-0)+2(0+1)+4(0+3) \\\\  & =6+2+12 \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(-4-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21}=\\frac{1}{20}\\cdot 4=\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7576155e-753f-578e-a4ec-c1e146863345" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285876} {:answer/id #uuid "7804ba9f-5287-5069-b31b-fbfc92859355" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285906} {:answer/id #uuid "94a9a448-efa8-5e13-8fb2-e9929ad565e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286140} {:answer/id #uuid "e6986340-6e6f-5163-a46c-b7ce43a43001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286898} {:answer/id #uuid "ff4f3922-637f-578e-9c1d-529afc788b0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287128}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186285906} :answer-field/id #uuid "00f3d5af-0a6c-5449-9acd-f6ef2a68a144" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287139}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "882c4c5b-7c6a-5276-989d-a6c4749ae87b" :question/math-academy-id "q-18280" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & =5\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =5(0-2)+0+3(-2+3) \\\\  & =-10+0+3 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{33}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{33}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{33} & =(-1)^{3+3}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-15-0 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{33}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{33}=\\frac{1}{-7}\\cdot (-15)=\\frac{15}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98a8da6d-1175-5690-993a-43baccf86886" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & -7 \\\\ 9 & 34 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059311} {:answer/id #uuid "f014818e-2156-5a3a-87fa-7de07564038f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -17 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059312} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb55f38-7b19-5ec2-a20e-0619df019195" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 22\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059313} {:answer/id #uuid "024ee0a8-81d1-5cf5-88b6-d174054fe95b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059314} {:answer/id #uuid "0cb34a7e-fbec-5611-b9f0-1ee391be7f83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -8 & -5 \\\\ -3 & -11 & -7 \\\\ 9 & 34 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059315}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059314} :answer-field/id #uuid "c87f3345-8202-5bf7-acde-2b4ceb74f385" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059310}] :question/id #uuid "ea75b5a7-9da3-5be1-8c64-31ab48a8aa3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-9681" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$." :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A$.\n\n$$\n\\det(A)=(7)(-2)+(2)(3)+(1)(9)=1.\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of minors. Delete row $i$ and column $j$ to obtain $M_{ij}$. For example,\n\n$$\nM_{11}=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix}=-2.\n$$\n\nComputing the remaining minors gives\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -3 & 9 \\\\ -8 & -11 & 34 \\\\ -5 & -7 & 21\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Apply the alternating signs $(-1)^{i+j}$ to form the cofactor matrix.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -34 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 21\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Transpose the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\nC^T=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Divide by the nonzero determinant.\n\n$$\nA^{-1}=\\frac{1}{\\det(A)}C^T=1\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -11 & 7 \\\\ 9 & -34 & 21\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060450 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0315a0c1-8e93-55c4-b28a-30f0ae9610cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357784} {:answer/id #uuid "77c1dc2e-024e-5c4b-beb2-f733502ac77d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358787} {:answer/id #uuid "7ff9ce2a-cbe8-5d79-93a4-76f40fb9e37b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358869} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4d33c6-a100-512f-a9be-112dbf385d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358957} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d1af3f-8416-5b82-9e39-9309a5040a16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359523}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186358869} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d9ac11a-04f8-5372-b25f-a5363dbf63f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "20571cf0-076d-5c7b-a788-d7a5f5cb703e" :question/math-academy-id "q-9710" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ k & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $18.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ k & 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix} & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ k & 0\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ k & 6\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(0-24)-2(0-4k)+3(0-k) \\\\  & =8k-3k-24 \\\\  & =5k-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(0-18) \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5k-24}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{5k-24}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=18$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{18}{5k-24} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{1}{5k-24} & =1 \\\\ 1 & =5k-24 \\\\ 25 & =5k \\\\ k & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060458 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e2e2a7fa-1a07-507e-9cfb-d555fed4d92f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 5 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059371} {:answer/id #uuid "413612e5-67ec-5bfe-a7b4-1ae63f30a529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -7 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059372} {:answer/id #uuid "4c1f7f26-d02f-5e3f-a75e-088281efd141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059373} {:answer/id #uuid "4f81fba0-53c1-5618-97a3-e5a601c25bd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059374} {:answer/id #uuid "4fa3e0c4-2a51-5f34-aca2-36798ca2ba7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059375}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059375} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e2f5d0b-4478-5dc8-803a-bd9eeb731d12" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "86bd8759-9672-5297-874b-c9bf15a86252" :question/math-academy-id "q-9965" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A) = 5$." :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** Find the determinant of $A$.\n\n$$\n\\det(A)=(1)(5)+(-1)(-6)+(3)(-2)=5.\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of minors. Delete row $i$ and column $j$ to obtain $M_{ij}$. For example,\n\n$$\nM_{11}=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}=5.\n$$\n\nComputing the remaining minors gives\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7 & -4 \\\\ -5 & -4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Apply the alternating signs $(-1)^{i+j}$ to form the cofactor matrix.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -6 & -2 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Transpose the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\nC^T=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Divide by the nonzero determinant.\n\n$$\nA^{-1}=\\frac{1}{\\det(A)}C^T=\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -5 \\\\ -6 & 7 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ - \\frac{6}{5} & \\frac{7}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ - \\frac{2}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060459 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e65ae8a-57ce-5eb7-8254-bbe131d8f40c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059377} {:answer/id #uuid "b31705b8-2e69-5452-b12a-9cd85d22b26a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059378} {:answer/id #uuid "ff8b60ca-2038-56d9-bf33-2d7df3d1d28d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059379} {:answer/id #uuid "1c2241db-dca5-5b98-b283-c76148dd792e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059380} {:answer/id #uuid "58134502-f6c0-5d83-9274-d6f7f28fca66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059381}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059377} :answer-field/id #uuid "168f3dd3-003b-54d0-ae3c-e643ac553095" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186059376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c04effc9-bb43-5aa7-be8b-3e036c90cdc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-9997" :question/problem "The entry $a_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & k & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $-1$ and $det(A) = 4 - 4k$. Find the value of $k$." :question/worked-solution "Since $A^{-1}=\\dfrac{1}{\\det(A)}C^T,$ the entry $a_{23}^{\\prime}$ uses the cofactor $C_{32}$. Remove row $3$ and column $2$ to get\n\n$$\nC_{32}=(-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix}=-4.\n$$\n\nUsing the given determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\na_{23}^{\\prime}=\\frac{-4}{4-4k}.\n$$\n\nThe inverse exists only when $k\\ne1$. Set this entry equal to $-1$ and solve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-4}{4-4k}&=-1\\\\-4&=-4+4k\\\\k&=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt $k=0,$ the determinant is $4\\ne0,$ so this value is valid."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087508 :question/id #uuid "318fc39e-0efe-5b98-968c-ff4408706471" :question/math-academy-id "e-4502" :question/problem "Calculate $A^{-1},$ where\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}{\\color{blue}{1}} & 0 \\\\ -2 & {\\color{red}{1}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2 \\times 2$ matrix\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A =\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\det(A) = 1 \\cdot 1 - 0 \\cdot (-2) = 1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix}. \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -0 \\\\ -(-2) & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087509 :question/id #uuid "195d7dab-edf2-536b-a7b7-d1c16c7b1071" :question/math-academy-id "e-4503" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\n\\det({A})=1 \\cdot 1 - 1 \\cdot 1 = 0.\n$$\n\nBecause $\\det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\n\\det({C})=3 \\cdot 3 - (-3) \\cdot 3 = 18.\n$$\n\nBecause $\\det(C) \\neq 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087510 :question/id #uuid "ef06dd89-501b-5d2b-a56d-4554a049a91d" :question/math-academy-id "e-4504" :question/problem "If \n$$\n\\displaystyle A =\n \\begin{bmatrix}1-k & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-k\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $\\det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(1-k)(1-k)-4 \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-2k-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-2k-3 & =0 \\\\ (k-3)(k+1) & =0 \\\\ k & =3,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $k$ are $k=3$ and $k=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b6b2951-5fda-53c8-896a-8bde83921b7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459437} {:answer/id #uuid "c82dca82-40a1-54e5-8fe2-071a3a53d264" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459438}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459437} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c97d18a-669f-55a0-ae63-6af35a70edb2" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460585} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6411512f-7951-596a-b5a9-6237363cf23b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459439} {:answer/id #uuid "b589497c-aaa2-56ee-9385-1f32f8cc20e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459440}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459439} :answer-field/id #uuid "7db0dbb8-05ee-56da-a79d-d8bf4fa9497d" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460586} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb6ed13f-8fd7-53ba-8290-837d992b005f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459441} {:answer/id #uuid "da8baa64-f2af-5f17-8355-f4e19addbcd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459442}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459442} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b3bde15-dda9-5eec-8013-c3084007af6f" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "dd3fba16-5fcc-50bc-8866-44ee67a3b9b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-11718" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible. Since $C$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $C$ is singular.\n\nTherefore, only $C$ is singular."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a320573-387a-58d0-a0b4-fdc4235e8e20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084675} {:answer/id #uuid "b777fb43-93d7-5dc7-a4cd-7e540ebf1199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = ± 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084676} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2c3fcb-2ccc-509d-8f4e-73dfead21b8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = ± 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084677} {:answer/id #uuid "f2eeec69-0a0d-5c28-bc9b-bdbb673c7f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k = 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084678} {:answer/id #uuid "084389ec-184e-56fd-a7b7-39ad8aa9eec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k =-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084679}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084676} :answer-field/id #uuid "b584fe55-a8c9-57cf-9bbb-cda45a7e1807" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084674}] :question/id #uuid "f2b7dccf-26ea-59f4-bdf6-7d70d461f4e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-11722" :question/problem "If $A = \\begin{bmatrix}k & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $k$." :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if its determinant is $0$. Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\det(A)=k\\cdot k-2\\cdot2=k^2-4.\n$$\n\nNow, set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k^2-4&=0\\\\(k-2)(k+2)&=0\\\\k&=2\\quad\\text{or}\\quad k=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\pm2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "419dd4e5-12cc-5539-9ce1-12dbb328e826" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251098} {:answer/id #uuid "7e26377c-0b5f-5e88-8cee-a0c378d66f48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251612} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d02b22-933b-5127-9e49-db343d3d3057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251946} {:answer/id #uuid "e9173fd7-88e5-5605-babf-0c1896274065" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252591} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a703d4-42c5-5789-b2d3-b2087a71eba0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252720}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251946} :answer-field/id #uuid "73272f9c-f427-56d0-a21e-b2927edff5b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253010}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ee61babb-f6b1-5a98-9886-55df60a724bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-11723" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}k & k \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =k\\cdot 1-k\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =k-2k \\\\  & =-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-k & =0 \\\\ k & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $k$ is $k=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99efa492-13f6-5efe-ab79-2c0e6743fb7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084687} {:answer/id #uuid "a464bdcf-7250-58c6-b8c6-f37fa6d9b9a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084688} {:answer/id #uuid "b0947fbe-5d11-5488-b8ed-5a04c3996918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It does not have an inverse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084689} {:answer/id #uuid "e3aff7b1-084a-5e43-8db7-06378b6bd625" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084690} {:answer/id #uuid "4490c64a-12f1-543c-aad6-26823e53dc68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084691}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186084690} :answer-field/id #uuid "441b7a62-f310-59e7-9c6c-330ce28188f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084686}] :question/id #uuid "a288b7d1-dd0e-57aa-80a7-821c89798323" :question/math-academy-id "q-11724" :question/problem "Calculate $A^{-1}$, where\n$$\n\\displaystyle A = \\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times2$ matrix, use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{bmatrix}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{ad-bc}\\begin{bmatrix}d&-b\\\\-c&a\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, compute the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\det(A)=(7)(1)-(2)(4)=-1.\n$$\n\nSince the determinant is nonzero, the inverse exists. Thus,\n\n$$\nA^{-1}=\\frac{1}{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying in either order gives the identity matrix, which verifies the result."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c0a8452-772e-5183-968e-5081778d81a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459443} {:answer/id #uuid "16964185-0fa1-5c40-ba30-02add50a42e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459444}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459444} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d7d1630-9e25-5340-bd4c-d1503c868d24" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460588} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c49f134d-b275-58ab-85af-ec9fd2b5885b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459445} {:answer/id #uuid "e352c568-e812-5e17-b65a-6e55c2065821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459446}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459446} :answer-field/id #uuid "91e63b07-cfa6-51d4-9446-17be269137d3" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460589} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cd74d9f-29c9-5af3-86e7-5d73dd7bfffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459447} {:answer/id #uuid "20983efb-be24-5fea-9f77-4785c48e9e97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459448}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459447} :answer-field/id #uuid "18e9fed9-651b-5bfd-9db4-7ea966e44fd6" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460590}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d6fdbc09-a579-52c0-b98c-5f14a5229abc" :question/math-academy-id "q-11725" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=6\\cdot 4-8\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)=0,$ we conclude that $B$ is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=(-1)\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 5=-10.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ do not have an inverse."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088369 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cd6adae-e9f3-524a-b8bf-48ef75173cdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086868} {:answer/id #uuid "fc5dce26-1de2-50e8-a61f-cf75e2936cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086869} {:answer/id #uuid "10c183f6-da00-5e11-b123-daf52b029ec0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086870} {:answer/id #uuid "1314bf11-24ec-50c5-bcb7-0fdd9e2c9a1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086871} {:answer/id #uuid "27dc674b-f8b0-5760-bc32-7f971a1ea37e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "It does not have an inverse" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086872}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186086869} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd13a2e2-a794-5e41-825a-de0f33392aab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086867}] :question/id #uuid "d70401ae-dfdb-5d0d-9525-7d09c6159753" :question/math-academy-id "q-7924" :question/problem "Calculate $Z^{-1}$ where\n$$\n\\displaystyle Z = \\begin{bmatrix}9 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times2$ matrix, use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{bmatrix}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{ad-bc}\\begin{bmatrix}d&-b\\\\-c&a\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFirst, compute the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\det(Z)=(9)(1)-(-1)(2)=11.\n$$\n\nSince the determinant is nonzero, the inverse exists. Thus,\n\n$$\nZ^{-1}=\\frac{1}{11}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{11} & \\frac{1}{11} \\\\ - \\frac{2}{11} & \\frac{9}{11}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying in either order gives the identity matrix, which verifies the result."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115062 :question/id #uuid "87bf279f-9f78-54cb-b9c3-e1bf1c5426ff" :question/math-academy-id "e-4505" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x &=5 \\\\ -5x+6y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation. The variable $y$ does not appear in the first equation, but this just means its coefficient is $0.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+0y &=5 \\\\ -5x+6y &=-8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\nA = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}2 & 0 \\\\ - 5 & 6\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}5 \\\\ - 8\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}2 & 0 \\\\ - 5 & 6\\end{array} \\right]}\n\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}5 \\\\ - 8\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115063 :question/id #uuid "359f4b72-60d2-54e2-b7ef-c48f1e3af708" :question/math-academy-id "e-4506" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5y &=-3x \\\\ 6+x &=-2+y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-5y &=0 \\\\ x-y &=-8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\nA = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}3 & - 5 \\\\ 1 & - 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ - 8\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}3 & - 5 \\\\ 1 & - 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}0 \\\\ - 8\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115064 :question/id #uuid "b87aa5eb-f689-5f34-baeb-f97c3f200552" :question/math-academy-id "e-4507" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}10 & - 15 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{array} \\right]}\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}5 \\\\ - 2\\end{array} \\right]}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}10x-15y &=5 \\\\ 1x+0y &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y &=1 \\\\ x &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115492 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac702230-e0b6-5149-946f-efd4c6240c5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111962} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d139bd-6d1e-5f66-a303-7e6b7a0e51de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111963} {:answer/id #uuid "d2848f95-94e5-5ab3-a01f-412463cb5507" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111964} {:answer/id #uuid "02c5947d-7aa5-5ba5-a47b-e026a2989d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111965} {:answer/id #uuid "70c3eeea-3b68-5006-bd47-787332cbacad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111966}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111962} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5747825-fbaf-5c36-b201-e23205e21435" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111961}] :question/id #uuid "ebdaa38a-80f3-5181-996b-ca5c169aa5a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-11979" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{array}{r}\\displaystyle \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}\\displaystyle 3 x + 5 y = 4 \\\\ \\displaystyle x - 7 y = - 4\\end{array} \\right. \\end{array}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, write the system with the variables ordered $x,y$ on the left and the constants on the right. Insert a zero coefficient for any missing variable.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3 x + 5 y &=4 \\\\ x - 7 y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -7\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{x}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nEach row of $A$ contains the coefficients from the corresponding equation. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115493 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a223b0ba-cc0b-5488-b008-a5a33b2c2c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111968} {:answer/id #uuid "da2e69a5-cf6f-57d2-8d67-6bb25c167d94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111969} {:answer/id #uuid "ee5978af-c54e-596d-9642-e6db91c6d113" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111970} {:answer/id #uuid "31eefa3e-ed3a-5aff-86ff-364467e08fa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111971} {:answer/id #uuid "5eca5f73-c48b-5682-bc09-1cce81fbb4cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111972}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111969} :answer-field/id #uuid "67908db4-252d-5747-9818-1cf87b96d68d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186111967}] :question/id #uuid "1ae858d6-0d70-54f7-a023-67b6c0b13f2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-12288" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{array}{r}\\displaystyle \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}\\displaystyle 2 y = 3 \\\\ \\displaystyle x = 0\\end{array} \\right. \\end{array}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, write the system with the variables ordered $x,y$ on the left and the constants on the right. Insert a zero coefficient for any missing variable.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2 y &=3 \\\\ x &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{x}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nEach row of $A$ contains the coefficients from the corresponding equation. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115732 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "886f8fb4-19fc-5428-98a2-3522bdf57b90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113359} {:answer/id #uuid "8eada92f-7290-511c-ac0d-3699fca3e681" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113360} {:answer/id #uuid "d0829c08-ca54-56ee-9dd0-dbacc0ce6e49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113361} {:answer/id #uuid "ec2b98e9-54be-57be-a5be-e6bbcb0f4cf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113362} {:answer/id #uuid "5c7d2242-a652-5592-a077-e9c3a917780a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113363}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186113362} :answer-field/id #uuid "db161969-3909-540d-9bda-f153f7134ab2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113358}] :question/id #uuid "0468eabf-1364-5afc-8b00-c2d28bd74d7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-31874" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{array}{r}\\displaystyle \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}\\displaystyle y + 3 x - 8 = 2 \\\\ \\displaystyle y + 9 = 5\\end{array} \\right. \\end{array}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, write the system with the variables ordered $x,y$ on the left and the constants on the right. Insert a zero coefficient for any missing variable.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3 x + y &=10 \\\\ y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{x}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nEach row of $A$ contains the coefficients from the corresponding equation. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115733 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "844af2ff-91bd-5774-977a-c4b75a56b7e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y &=-7 \\\\ x &=10\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298123} {:answer/id #uuid "ba86e523-ab11-5712-a0ef-e9273fbba9ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y &=10 \\\\ y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298364} {:answer/id #uuid "c0094f31-2ab1-54a0-a168-daab0cf20812" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+5y &=10 \\\\ y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298399} {:answer/id #uuid "f1959011-ff17-5b5f-bab6-775af7511c23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y &=-7 \\\\ x &=10\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298574} {:answer/id #uuid "f197b44a-bdc4-5917-8017-c00985501ea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y &=10 \\\\ x &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298575}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186298575} :answer-field/id #uuid "62cbb4a6-4bc5-5953-a9a5-b4146109a185" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298969}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d80073fa-9f5d-593f-a765-d5bf9c3d142b" :question/math-academy-id "q-31876" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y &=10 \\\\ x+0y &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y &=10 \\\\ x &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115740 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c75a7b4-8cf8-5814-905e-316cf670a3c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{array}{r}\\displaystyle \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}\\displaystyle 3 x + 2 y = 1 \\\\ \\displaystyle x = - 2\\end{array} \\right. \\end{array}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113407} {:answer/id #uuid "deda1f91-6fc0-5da8-bca9-765394cc5db3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{array}{r}\\displaystyle \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}\\displaystyle 9 x + 6 y = - 1 \\\\ \\displaystyle x = - 2\\end{array} \\right. \\end{array}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113408} {:answer/id #uuid "f05adb6e-e4fd-54ee-a877-80be7e74409e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{array}{r}\\displaystyle \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}\\displaystyle 3 x + 2 y = - 1 \\\\ \\displaystyle x = - 2\\end{array} \\right. \\end{array}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113409} {:answer/id #uuid "f761650d-2720-5b17-8f25-48a1bb41f74b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{array}{r}\\displaystyle \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}\\displaystyle 9 x + 6 y = 3 \\\\ \\displaystyle x + y = - 2\\end{array} \\right. \\end{array}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113410} {:answer/id #uuid "3b491284-60c9-534a-a93b-663a44d5a865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{array}{r}\\displaystyle \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}\\displaystyle 9 x + 6 y - 3 = 0 \\\\ \\displaystyle x - 2 = 0\\end{array} \\right. \\end{array}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113411}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186113409} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca7d485d-e01a-5fee-be3e-8b54af74ae8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113406}] :question/id #uuid "35b88fb0-9cd6-5ac5-a270-9cfdc3fa43ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-32020" :question/problem "What is the system of equations represented by\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$?" :question/worked-solution "Multiplying the coefficient matrix by the column vector of variables gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 x + 6 y \\\\ x\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}9x+6y &=-3\\\\x &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDividing the first equation by $3$ gives the equivalent system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=-1\\\\x &=-2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115977 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb33624c-6be3-586c-9f4c-c074a27c7f0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114800} {:answer/id #uuid "09835377-925f-53b0-8db2-15c8f9035baf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114801} {:answer/id #uuid "14bf7db7-1afb-5197-8e09-66ebf25f2d4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114802} {:answer/id #uuid "48086d77-a5d6-57a3-ad13-850af3a4afaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114803} {:answer/id #uuid "57e6ed06-d447-576f-b98d-16a2b47babc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114804}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114801} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4695ddb-2096-52b3-bdb5-b21fed97be19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186114799}] :question/id #uuid "de8294a6-a6d8-531a-8dfa-e94ae37b28f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-8818" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\begin{array}{r}\\displaystyle \\left\\{  \\begin{array}{l}\\displaystyle 2 y - 7 x = 3 \\\\ \\displaystyle - x + 2 y = - 1\\end{array} \\right. \\end{array}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, write the system with the variables ordered $x,y$ on the left and the constants on the right. Insert a zero coefficient for any missing variable.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}- 7 x + 2 y &=3 \\\\ - x + 2 y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{x}=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix},\\qquad\\mathbf{b}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nEach row of $A$ contains the coefficients from the corresponding equation. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119595 :question/id #uuid "3545b168-5226-5f47-ac0d-3ff5509e866e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4447" :question/problem "What is the minor of $a_{13}$ in \n$$\nA=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cccc}0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 0 & - 1 \\\\ - 6 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{array} \\right]}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get the minor of $a_{13}$, we remove the $1$st row and $3$rd column:\n\n$$\nA=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cccc}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}2} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 5 & 1 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & - 1 \\\\ - 6 & 3 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\nM_{13}=\n{\\left| \\begin{array}{ccc}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & - 1 \\\\ - 6 & 3 & 0\\end{array} \\right|}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119596 :question/id #uuid "8e61e639-f165-5157-91c0-e9a6faf734a6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4448" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of $d_{23}$ in \n$$\nD=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cccc}0 & 2 & 3 & - 6 \\\\ 7 & - 3 & - 2 & - 1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 8 & 9 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 0 & 0\\end{array} \\right]}\n.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of $d_{23}$, we remove the $2$nd row and $3$rd column:\n\n$$\nD=\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cccc}0 & 2 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & - 6 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}- 2} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 6 & 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 9 \\\\ 5 & 4 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\nM_{23}=\n\t\\left|\n\t{\\begin{array}{ccc}0 & 2 & - 6 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 0\\end{array}}\n\t\\right|.\n$$\n\nNow, the cofactor of $d_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}{M}_{23} \\\\  & =-{M}_{23} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 5 & 4 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119597 :question/id #uuid "3e091496-053c-59fb-90d6-d8fb89ea6004" :question/math-academy-id "e-4449" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\nA=\n\\left[\n\t{\\begin{array}{cccc}0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & 0 & - 1 \\\\ - 6 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{array}}\n\\right].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & ={a}_{11}{C}_{11}+{a}_{12}{C}_{12}+{a}_{13}{C}_{13}+{a}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+2\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =2{C}_{13} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}∗ & ∗ & 2 & ∗ \\\\ 5 & 1 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & ∗ & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & ∗ & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2(-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\left(5\\begin{vmatrix}6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =2(5(6\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 3)-(1\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-6))+0(1\\cdot 3-6\\cdot (-6))) \\\\  & =2(15+6+0) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 21 \\\\  & =42\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120207 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0843f07d-7e63-5667-aa53-1128919652ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299971} {:answer/id #uuid "0cd7cf2f-5a7d-5888-8851-073bfc651c1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299999} {:answer/id #uuid "279ddaf4-4285-58dd-9d16-ab377c009e2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "112" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300151} {:answer/id #uuid "2c0fdb8f-cde8-5eb3-81e4-70beaa668e51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300176} {:answer/id #uuid "3243cc72-8722-5358-b43b-c8b6ceed365e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300211}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186300151} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b52385f-d14f-5531-974a-819f1b812a30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301564}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4807bb32-2a62-536d-a90f-b629a70d8fa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-32800" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & ={a}_{11}{C}_{11}+{a}_{12}{C}_{12}+{a}_{13}{C}_{13}+{a}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =0\\cdot {C}_{11}+8\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+0\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =8{C}_{12} \\\\  & =8\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}8} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ -1 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =8(-1)^{1+2}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-8\\left((-1)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix}+0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =8(6\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2)-0+0 \\\\  & =8\\cdot 14 \\\\  & =112\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120400 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b4410b8-f0e4-58de-9edc-5668a5589faf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321738} {:answer/id #uuid "921be6d6-293c-5f86-bb3a-4c6e89e3eae4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322306} {:answer/id #uuid "957cfae7-9311-525e-a752-55375485f3f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322338} {:answer/id #uuid "978cdfc9-3483-5d36-b58c-045a19eafe7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322355} {:answer/id #uuid "a9ea0575-76eb-514c-ae64-98c42fd95990" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322482}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321738} :answer-field/id #uuid "22b84cc8-5f7c-568c-be16-eefd456d61f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "485535b5-374e-549b-93f0-b8a241d934fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-36031" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of ${a}_{23}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -7 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 0 & 11 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of ${a}_{23}$, we remove the $2$nd row and $3$rd column: \n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -7 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 3 \\\\ {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{{\\color{gray}0}} & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 9 & 0 & {\\color{gray}∗} & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{23}=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, the cofactor of ${a}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}{M}_{23} \\\\  & =-{M}_{23} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -7 & 3 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120401 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44a53c04-e529-5980-9871-488b48753234" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "125" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321687} {:answer/id #uuid "705109d1-3af4-5ff3-acf7-5d3d0f081f00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-218" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322023} {:answer/id #uuid "70f2e27b-b69d-5a8e-a251-9c44a0969327" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-197" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322031} {:answer/id #uuid "825d1898-c1c5-515c-8d32-7d9391d79b76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-255" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322174} {:answer/id #uuid "fd14dd4b-300e-50c6-82b4-70959e79fea7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "315" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323143}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186322174} :answer-field/id #uuid "9edb3717-adce-570c-8b92-ef6311946dc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323478}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5f3bd215-2eb4-5f41-af3f-5119c1a64176" :question/math-academy-id "q-36055" :question/problem "Calculate the determinant of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We use the cofactor expansion along the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & ={a}_{11}{C}_{11}+{a}_{12}{C}_{12}+{a}_{13}{C}_{13}+{a}_{14}{C}_{14} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot {C}_{11}+0\\cdot {C}_{12}+0\\cdot {C}_{13}+5\\cdot {C}_{14} \\\\  & =-3{C}_{11}+5{C}_{14} \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}-3} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ {\\color{lightgray}∗} & 6 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+5\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}{\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}∗} & {\\color{lightgray}5} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 & {\\color{lightgray}∗} \\\\ -1 & 6 & 0 & {\\color{lightgray}∗}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-3)(-1)^{1+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+5(-1)^{1+4}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-5\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-3\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -3 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-2\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & -5\\left(0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{vmatrix}-0\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{vmatrix}+3\\cdot \\begin{vmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{vmatrix}\\right) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot (-3\\cdot (0+18)+(-2)\\cdot (0-12))-5\\cdot (3\\cdot (24-1)) \\\\  & =90-345 \\\\  & =-255\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120505 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1d807f2-dde8-5fe6-91f0-a64a98f87d3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119145} {:answer/id #uuid "d7819dc8-3b55-5e27-9b43-98341fe85160" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119146} {:answer/id #uuid "4b187043-523b-505e-a291-645b3579add5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119147} {:answer/id #uuid "50f8547c-b0c8-5b2f-9eff-d871d0826ecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}5 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119148} {:answer/id #uuid "7bb6d1f4-9c0b-5a45-93b8-b9e3bd9137c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119149}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119149} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8f15969-c4d1-5f41-9777-694bcc1cd2ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119144}] :question/id #uuid "28c1749e-69a3-5820-b219-3a0e2c91ffd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-69959" :question/problem "Find the cofactor of $d_{33}$ in $$\n\\displaystyle D = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 9 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, to get the minor of $d_{33}$, remove the $3$rd row and $3$rd column:\n\n$$\nM_{33}=\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe cofactor includes the alternating sign $(-1)^{i+j}$. Therefore,\n\n$$\nC_{33}=(-1)^{3+3}M_{33}=M_{33}=\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -7\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120509 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08273a7b-1bac-5a99-93b3-8f8cb788c45a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336099} {:answer/id #uuid "196885bf-dac5-5878-a8c0-5723f143ab2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336268} {:answer/id #uuid "22092397-4007-5e20-b20b-f97d690ed48b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336350} {:answer/id #uuid "72397941-6b44-5027-93ce-decb6920b741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337054} {:answer/id #uuid "e012a316-8efb-545e-abc5-8b3f3fd57895" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337990}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336099} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bc53fd8-34d2-53ce-9867-d846eedc2933" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fdc0941d-7700-5e04-b45b-b1b70aba9ef5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71017" :question/problem "What is the minor of ${x}_{33}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle X=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get the minor of ${x}_{33}$, we remove the $3$rd row and $3$rd column:\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 3 \\\\ {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-1} & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ 1 & 4 & {\\color{gray}∗} & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{33}=\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120510 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0adee605-6c5c-52e7-bc1f-9a014cac151f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 8 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336135} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ca4fbf-5483-5bff-b68e-1df192b4f870" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337669} {:answer/id #uuid "bdcd5c10-38ee-57ef-b2e9-0aa20426e21a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337718} {:answer/id #uuid "c779c75f-52e0-59b1-a4cb-55d98c009253" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 8 & 0\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337801} {:answer/id #uuid "f04b92dc-3f0e-593e-aac0-cb6ff5666ec4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 9 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338132}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186337669} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f218c2a-1200-574a-bf1c-16ecea1cbe54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "57c18875-2f75-5f94-849f-d4b4a9525a98" :question/math-academy-id "q-71018" :question/problem "Find the minor of ${q}_{23}$ in \n$$\n\\displaystyle Q=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 9 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To get the minor of  ${q}_{23}$, we remove the $2$nd row and $3$rd column:\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 1 \\\\ {\\color{gray}∗} & {\\color{gray}∗} & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{1} & {\\color{gray}∗} \\\\ -1 & 1 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & {\\color{gray}∗} & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the minor is \n\n$$\n{M}_{23}=\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 0\\end{vmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240804 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "037393f2-b6d0-5f15-83d8-ecc1860d366c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238112} {:answer/id #uuid "6ab2f7b0-2737-5b4c-bbd9-35ee06e4f051" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238979} {:answer/id #uuid "6e0bd746-222a-5820-82fc-3ca96f0e2566" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239002} {:answer/id #uuid "d9eb1982-ea08-5419-a703-c8a1cd07e7c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239957} {:answer/id #uuid "ff00e538-8c1b-580a-b72d-811689b8542b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240313}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186239002} :answer-field/id #uuid "703ead68-58ab-5b1c-a34a-4f9cab386dc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0b281857-5cf5-5dda-b8cb-bae31f90bde6" :question/math-academy-id "q-104134" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\ngiven that $det(A)=-1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's follow the standard five-step procedure.\n\n**Step 1:** We are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Form the matrix of the minors of $A.$\nTo make this matrix, we replace each entry of $A$ by its minor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & \\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Create the matrix of cofactors by changing the sign of some of the entries of $M$ according to the rule of alternating signs.\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Write down the transpose of the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n**Step 5:** Use the formula for the inverse of a $3\\times 3$ matrix.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240871 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "318e4ff1-9eda-5227-97de-069fe65726f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238485} {:answer/id #uuid "581fb52d-c562-5a61-83a7-0ccc875e2d6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238814} {:answer/id #uuid "852c2a15-9bb2-5c2f-a3f3-70dc20643dc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239213} {:answer/id #uuid "99946c30-ae52-50d2-ab9b-73478b6df019" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239388} {:answer/id #uuid "c135f6ba-7057-5a82-9972-767caa7e7342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239744}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186239388} :answer-field/id #uuid "05ee2e28-0127-5de7-9d19-9359e9043495" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240334}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "fc11b8c2-85be-59ad-bbca-214a365781c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-104413" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =3\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3(1-0)-0+(-1-0) \\\\  & =3+0-1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{23}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{32} & =(-1)^{3+2}\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(0-1) \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{23}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 1=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240874 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "321b8d3b-cd54-5aec-b3c6-614d9119d85e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238490} {:answer/id #uuid "82f83531-f2a4-50ef-b8cf-747f2110b4e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239195} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a62450-4a64-5b83-97a1-956b91c29de7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239765} {:answer/id #uuid "c3910286-f59a-54dd-9194-1920e9c24f46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239783} {:answer/id #uuid "efe95074-4ae4-5190-923c-417bab521d7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240167}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186239765} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c312751-eff3-5874-b792-a6fa94261128" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "d6189c9e-c299-5fe1-934e-c85b7854108f" :question/math-academy-id "q-104416" :question/problem "Determine the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix $A$ $=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}A=\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+0\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(2+1)-(1-2)+0 \\\\  & =-3+1+0 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{31}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{13} & =(-1)^{1+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-1-4 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{31}^{′}=\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}=\\frac{1}{-2}\\cdot (-5)=\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0823e679-5623-5513-8197-33a1c8ae8c23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238141} {:answer/id #uuid "4ef0a0c8-e834-5d68-a259-7fedd6fed2b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238732} {:answer/id #uuid "6c5fede8-1aad-5729-9d8a-208e730ea058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238989} {:answer/id #uuid "e74baa48-26f8-5695-bad5-d271d1e3e38f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240091} {:answer/id #uuid "fa084b2e-50e1-5131-aea7-50c9409524aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240265}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238732} :answer-field/id #uuid "65817036-87eb-5cc8-80d8-f7e75f7b7758" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "57a186fd-b1ba-539f-bb9d-e1998b570fc0" :question/math-academy-id "q-104428" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ k & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $det(A)=2k+2.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=2k+2\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(0-2) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2k+2}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{12}^{′}=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k+1} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ k+1 & =2 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3541fac5-1091-5ae2-a5ad-314c1f884760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238516} {:answer/id #uuid "5ae53416-c44d-546d-8f7e-7708603910aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238842} {:answer/id #uuid "6328ad49-14be-5303-988b-aaee411b7a0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238926} {:answer/id #uuid "eb9f65d2-628a-5c01-b36e-b3ccb0b68a33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240128} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a8d1a8-0d2d-581e-9482-a9f728baa3e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240216}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240216} :answer-field/id #uuid "57747a39-2687-5194-90fc-e0d6b4a69104" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "539f41b1-227f-56ae-b693-cf3443bf466c" :question/math-academy-id "q-104431" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & k \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $-1$ and $det(A)=4-2k.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=4-2k\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(2-0) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-2k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ 1 & =2-k \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3907885c-b8d9-5a8a-b101-b8bacd3c100c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238548} {:answer/id #uuid "59dc3dbc-a563-5ed7-a2b8-0b53ab3690df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238829} {:answer/id #uuid "7219f929-3c4c-5130-ba67-06b6ec68f6bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239034} {:answer/id #uuid "e1294134-a47b-51be-972a-dbe70aba54ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240033} {:answer/id #uuid "e666f6f4-3b9a-508e-addb-22f8d57a69de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240078}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238548} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d4629b7-d427-5661-a6f1-3af0b7b88fc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240464}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "55417378-dec5-552f-8b04-ebd15181a9f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-104439" :question/problem "The entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & k & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\nequals $-\\frac{1}{4}$ and $det(A)=k-4.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that we are given the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\ndet(A)=k-4\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{22}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{22}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{22} & =(-1)^{2+2}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{22}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{22} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-4}\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{k-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{22}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{4}$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{1}{k-4} \\\\ k-4 & =-4 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253311 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3458a089-3888-542e-968d-c9518a04e88d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461815} {:answer/id #uuid "50778f05-ddf5-582c-8db9-cc7782d783f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461816}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461816} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eca055b-5464-5837-a901-254ea6c3a13c" :answer-field/key "$H=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0abc8f03-a6b8-5309-9492-8dc139b5f6cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461817} {:answer/id #uuid "9c816193-4544-54b9-b7d7-6c9d022fe5bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461818}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461818} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cf477f3-ea09-51a1-9a9b-7b55b2cadfda" :answer-field/key "$J=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73ab26a4-2324-5b3c-8149-15706d53927d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461819} {:answer/id #uuid "f92a8eac-48f4-5940-81c5-cfc73dbdf656" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461820}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186461819} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d8dc630-97cd-5342-89aa-58a8996e2070" :answer-field/key "$K=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462663}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "87ca815d-8c8d-5ffa-9415-2a57d9bd87a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-11717" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $H$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(H)=5\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(H)=0,$ we conclude that $H$ is not invertible. Since $H$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $H$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $J$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(J)=2\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(J)=0,$ we conclude that $J$ is not invertible. Since $J$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $J$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $K$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\nTherefore, only $H$ and $J$ is singular."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "097794a2-c7ca-5ecf-bd92-2d6b9637edf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250639} {:answer/id #uuid "87862fd4-0b9f-5398-911d-63cce6d1b136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251692} {:answer/id #uuid "c745fe31-0cba-5f79-a40c-985ece6242bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252314} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e5419b-2e45-5470-ad3f-325c6e4e71dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252419} {:answer/id #uuid "e279ed19-5a71-5d13-9f8d-6703bfc76869" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252544}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250639} :answer-field/id #uuid "886a0983-97da-5781-96e9-27635821fd09" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253038}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "18e87006-2d52-52b3-8fdf-cef524aa5a2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-11719" :question/problem "If $F=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & t \\\\ t & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $F$ is singular if and only if $det(F)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(F) & =3\\cdot 3-t\\cdot t \\\\  & =9-{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =9 \\\\ t & =\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $t$ are $t=\\pm 3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253313 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57d016cc-b32a-556a-872a-d9d9454755e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251269} {:answer/id #uuid "7f24ab14-2022-5d0d-aa61-084ff480fc31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251621} {:answer/id #uuid "ac0e0abc-a204-57f0-a0ca-d651601dc526" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252047} {:answer/id #uuid "e207ec5b-404c-50f6-acae-784dfe8e282b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252541} {:answer/id #uuid "f8fa13d3-a4d7-5bb5-8a44-96e5e778acbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252733}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252047} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9e9e596-1625-5316-9294-354fbe58edae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e6398e19-0166-5ea2-9ff8-a93fab46629b" :question/math-academy-id "q-11721" :question/problem "If $Q=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ x & x\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $Q$ is singular if and only if $det(Q)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =3\\cdot x-x\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3x-6x \\\\  & =-3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x & =0 \\\\ x & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $x$ is $x=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "783db2fd-7825-5c2a-a37c-ecf12e9a46b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251550} {:answer/id #uuid "78c0bab0-9b03-5269-8dab-8e7ea4106e4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251554} {:answer/id #uuid "8c394e4f-1154-5d85-9535-8a7a4b1a9b74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251736} {:answer/id #uuid "9180c1c8-1f7c-540a-8d44-d585577c0e83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251795} {:answer/id #uuid "c3f59c7d-fd33-58d7-ae00-8babf85da183" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252288}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186251554} :answer-field/id #uuid "e38d674a-89c9-50fe-9a20-d74c11c871f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253196}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0c7b9ea7-cded-56a3-a2f3-1334f92c0300" :question/math-academy-id "q-11726" :question/problem "If $P=\\begin{bmatrix}n & -8 \\\\ -2 & n\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $n.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $P$ is singular if and only if $det(P)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =n\\cdot n-(-2)\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & ={n}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-16 & =0 \\\\ {n}^{2} & =16 \\\\ n & =\\pm 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $n$ are $n=\\pm 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256747 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "218ce074-ca3d-5510-94ae-15f6ed90c540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253968} {:answer/id #uuid "4ac890f0-a9d7-5b17-a40e-a5d265c117e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254312} {:answer/id #uuid "72520afb-7f21-542b-a3df-d45e415f22cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254683} {:answer/id #uuid "a1cb95dc-24db-531b-ad73-639a23776783" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255097} {:answer/id #uuid "aa7eeada-dbe5-547f-9c1d-1e0392b79546" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255177}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186255097} :answer-field/id #uuid "065e052d-4c76-5e45-8830-930b465810e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b54cfad2-6363-5425-bcc2-f4a9411e32b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-12291" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=y-1 \\\\ x &=-y+1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=-1 \\\\ x+y &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0374d4b9-d3f5-58bb-9722-96e77b28c1f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259906} {:answer/id #uuid "0ae9cf60-5da1-53a3-bf0f-ef78104194f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259974} {:answer/id #uuid "221a1f9e-48de-5ad2-b7a7-0cd0177337c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260171} {:answer/id #uuid "bcd7767a-0b24-520c-a516-0d1ec05dc43e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261541} {:answer/id #uuid "d8a87fed-62b4-50bd-a674-0ebc4ea306f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261784}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260171} :answer-field/id #uuid "f906eaf2-6afd-581e-857d-b8dfc0c79584" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262555}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f956f6a8-fa50-55df-aecf-a4883333e21d" :question/math-academy-id "q-127742" :question/problem "Calculate ${B}^{-1}$, where \n$$\n\\displaystyle B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $B$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(B)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(B)=2\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 1=-1\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(B)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B{B}^{-1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,{\\color{green}✓} \\\\ {B}^{-1}B & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,{\\color{green}✓}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262821 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bea1db8-d662-5dcf-87be-fe4836a83f51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260115} {:answer/id #uuid "52b9b812-f224-5881-889d-cbe9f61a1ac6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260575} {:answer/id #uuid "708d1507-59f4-58c9-a3dd-47ff44fc9f5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260864} {:answer/id #uuid "8f4a42e4-e53f-562c-8ce9-170d332d7a26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261123} {:answer/id #uuid "e51e6904-7944-5c3a-83ee-49118b169c50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261891}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260575} :answer-field/id #uuid "87d12d6a-9753-5d9b-b0f5-09780e5b79d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "298737fa-66e8-531a-9405-d90ed3d1ecd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127744" :question/problem "Calculate ${C}^{-1}$, where\n$$\n\\displaystyle C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $C$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(C)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(C)=3\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 3=-3\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(C)}\\begin{bmatrix}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-3)}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C{C}^{-1} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,{\\color{green}✓} \\\\ {C}^{-1}C & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,{\\color{green}✓}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262822 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83031cf0-e568-5359-b7ee-f956035ef639" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463634} {:answer/id #uuid "e4cf2a4d-34df-5aca-961e-fc888997d1ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463635}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463635} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdcbe749-383a-5cb7-9f78-d6159757abf9" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464751} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbb3d7ee-532c-5b06-b40b-f4c2dbe2d0d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463636} {:answer/id #uuid "eea6cd9f-fca7-5155-b38b-3664f40c5e11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463637}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463636} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5a898ab-fc64-534b-9fa2-a231d2f0b959" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464752} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "367796bf-a0ff-5cf6-9aaf-31902587b686" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463638} {:answer/id #uuid "0144a740-b964-5dd0-8cb7-ff3f206d1152" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463639}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463638} :answer-field/id #uuid "773e2d3e-4596-5ce9-b52a-b7bceb4276e2" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464753}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9987fa7a-d96a-5001-a5b8-b5e558e85078" :question/math-academy-id "q-127751" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=(-1)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 0=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=(-2)\\cdot 5-(-3)\\cdot (3)=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262823 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8c473f5-ef95-5227-a968-e2e86ab24e1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463640} {:answer/id #uuid "ef280a56-6aa4-5367-afd4-c488c98b4baa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463641}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463641} :answer-field/id #uuid "bce7c6c8-b9b1-552a-b5e1-0f6140ff2c88" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464754} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "929235db-049d-563d-9c46-3e63d1f2cabc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463642} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9297a7-d7f3-5f84-9db4-8e4456568e67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463643}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463642} :answer-field/id #uuid "48fb156a-09ce-5fde-8695-5588211123e1" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464755} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eb27b827-2491-5ec9-8772-7e647962fd24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463644} {:answer/id #uuid "da00eb55-ba67-5112-89f2-1681a8d1c68d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463645}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463645} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcd2d553-3e6c-5d1d-9ac4-1a5aba1b575d" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2e8059f3-ef63-587d-911b-0d0c0a784873" :question/math-academy-id "q-127755" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=0\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262824 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f57cf2ee-5c54-5728-9819-04ba25ccaed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463646} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe95562-995d-540a-a75b-c6729affad85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463647}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463646} :answer-field/id #uuid "09b46ce7-eeb0-59a8-90f1-679f8c0295ff" :answer-field/key "$S=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464757} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bde6b23b-b56d-5b3d-a341-8a7675217e27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463648} {:answer/id #uuid "306399cf-a4fb-5e1f-9e1c-fab262184a89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463649}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463649} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4b22761-b532-55a6-93c3-281e6baeea2e" :answer-field/key "$T=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464758} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad303f4b-49e7-5eb1-b038-2436daaa6d7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463650} {:answer/id #uuid "7e3babfc-5f8a-55a0-949b-758d8eacf432" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463651}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463650} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7b1f0e4-c9c9-5321-988b-aaf8e81cba4d" :answer-field/key "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464759}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "87b20497-ceac-5d64-8634-616821707ef5" :question/math-academy-id "q-127757" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $S$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(S)=1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0=-1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(S)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $S$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $T$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot (-6)-4\\cdot (-3)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(T)=0,$ we conclude that $T$ is not invertible. Since $T$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $T$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $U$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(U)=0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1)=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(U)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $U$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $T$ is singular."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262825 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d30b47ef-87b0-5e27-a184-0a096fd33124" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463652} {:answer/id #uuid "33d939ee-6d35-51bf-8bb9-1d48cd53e796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463653}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463653} :answer-field/id #uuid "13f6015b-077b-5764-a2dd-d3aae8b43612" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464760} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4af08d0a-5536-510f-abab-da5fdbdceb28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463654} {:answer/id #uuid "35d0cb07-478b-566b-9247-784f753b25b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463655}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463654} :answer-field/id #uuid "dedfc344-69b8-5863-a5ce-c4f18d91df8a" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464761} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9ccb9cb-9df6-55dc-8aff-1d3a958bab36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463656} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec3ad4b-8ef7-53f9-a9d2-9dabd3a7a706" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463657}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463657} :answer-field/id #uuid "189a8dad-81d9-534b-b8f8-9df3343a27e3" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 12 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c7dc44ce-440a-5f50-b6a8-db3db16e9582" :question/math-academy-id "q-127762" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- The matrix $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $B$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=4\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 3=2.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(B)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $B$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=4\\cdot 9-3\\cdot 12=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)=0,$ we conclude that $C$ is not invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $C$ do not have an inverse."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262826 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc10acc5-cbe4-5aa7-85e8-9d27a5cfe577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463658} {:answer/id #uuid "54ce08b8-b1b6-51d3-82c5-8ce0eae6a5df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463659}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463659} :answer-field/id #uuid "8037c49c-f8b0-55ab-9b8d-c0cab9f33665" :answer-field/key "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464763} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f65a48c6-d48a-5389-9967-5b20a96b30f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463660} {:answer/id #uuid "839aeca5-60b3-587e-9712-cc3955ffe0fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463661}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463660} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ae8dfdf-3ddf-57c5-b5be-6a6ce59947b9" :answer-field/key "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464764} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f467b224-40ff-5b05-86f0-3f8c1a836859" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463662} {:answer/id #uuid "efd8deea-90c9-5a2d-8712-50eac0029e38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463663}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463662} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bc783cb-7e9c-5966-ba24-f9cc38ab506c" :answer-field/key "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464765}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7be51f92-4cc3-51a8-b911-c18f52c55601" :question/math-academy-id "q-127821" :question/problem "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- For the matrix $A$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(A)=-2\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 6=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(A)=0,$ we conclude that $A$ is not invertible. Since $A$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $A$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\n- For the matrix $C$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(C)=1\\cdot 5-7\\cdot 0=5.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(C)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $C$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is singular."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262839 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c0752f8-54df-507a-872b-fce6c55fcc41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259989} {:answer/id #uuid "1b8f8217-73b8-5aac-bc6a-21c690404158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260111} {:answer/id #uuid "a0659982-c103-5f57-83fb-988b62210ec7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261268} {:answer/id #uuid "a7949e65-d752-55be-b89d-fa6d51459350" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261338} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb45516-48e8-5a7d-bb41-07e91dbcf8b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261669}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261268} :answer-field/id #uuid "de18e845-9fc1-5af4-bf61-8d1ea6725965" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "524e74d6-0355-574f-af8e-7809bad3676c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127899" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}k-1 & k-1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =(k-1)\\cdot (-1)-(k-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-k+1-3k+3 \\\\  & =-4k+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4k+4 & =0 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $k$ is $k=1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262840 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f0c10c6-3508-5550-98fd-f098d04bede5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260141} {:answer/id #uuid "3e8f1f21-9c81-5ef5-b4fe-0d20d66954ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260426} {:answer/id #uuid "66ed762d-bc10-5c9a-9a0d-59b6f60da393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260773} {:answer/id #uuid "beafacad-b185-562e-8397-0f520d94cd1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261557} {:answer/id #uuid "c4bf894e-96f1-598c-861b-46bd6ece34bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261612}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260426} :answer-field/id #uuid "909985c8-f2ff-5344-aacb-a238867289fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262379}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "49be873f-6aae-5fe9-b9e9-08cc0609f50a" :question/math-academy-id "q-127900" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}k & 3 \\\\ 27 & k\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =k\\cdot k-27\\cdot 3 \\\\  & ={k}^{2}-81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{k}^{2}-81 & =0 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =81 \\\\ k & =\\pm 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $k$ are $k=\\pm 9.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262841 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0694821e-0afc-5a6f-9ac3-c60009288f14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\pm 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259936} {:answer/id #uuid "82ad1107-f4f2-56fb-a170-26080bfb5a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\pm 9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261009} {:answer/id #uuid "93eed24a-7d3e-5252-8646-ba1e56d6756f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261161} {:answer/id #uuid "acb60d02-9af1-5edb-8a62-0a7f615d8394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261386} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b9c926-8614-5473-84ac-a0af3c07259f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "a=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261991}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259936} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5f9163f-3e19-52b4-9fae-e228093cfe55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "54a4b93b-d93e-5ce6-98ac-7b0ed79d28ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-127901" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}48 & a \\\\ a & 3\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $A$ is singular if and only if $det(A)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =48\\cdot 3-a\\cdot a \\\\  & =144-{a}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}144-{a}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =144 \\\\ a & =\\pm 12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $a$ are $a=\\pm 12.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262842 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e10364-a8ca-5a9b-8ec9-fb274ee07c3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259910} {:answer/id #uuid "64215484-b9df-5191-b8c1-9280990fe3aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260740} {:answer/id #uuid "b5950187-60d8-50ca-a7cc-6a821b22c615" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261470} {:answer/id #uuid "cec39778-4048-5806-ae58-6218823c031b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261705} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a62acf-b03a-52a7-ab5a-7633988a7413" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=\\pm 10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261728}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261470} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfd7d4c7-e60d-5c53-95c8-2c7046132a9a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a4d5dba8-4e64-55e3-a838-e85b88eeb6cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-127903" :question/problem "If $M=\\begin{bmatrix}t & 5 \\\\ t & 9\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot 9-t\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =9t-5t \\\\  & =4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262843 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3059120f-ca9e-51ca-9841-1f8df800e6d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260311} {:answer/id #uuid "5bf24db5-f1ae-5524-83bc-edf5d3ad239e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260659} {:answer/id #uuid "621ece07-1998-5006-b429-8870d6c0b314" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260720} {:answer/id #uuid "673bf1ec-9954-5f5f-b4e0-082e19a5ab7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260777} {:answer/id #uuid "929a515e-de47-5de2-b043-79d260b71667" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n=\\pm 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261149}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186261149} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1e9e066-1c72-5b37-a693-dbbf75cdc32f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "97157127-f9e4-550a-8517-ce69acd7410c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127905" :question/problem "If $P=\\begin{bmatrix}n & -4 \\\\ -16 & n\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value(s) of $n.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $P$ is singular if and only if $det(P)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =n\\cdot n-(-16)\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & ={n}^{2}-64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-64 & =0 \\\\ {n}^{2} & =64 \\\\ n & =\\pm 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $n$ are $n=\\pm 8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262844 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "327c9e3e-2327-51e3-ab75-0eb4d6685f48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260330} {:answer/id #uuid "5528c44b-359f-5f31-ae64-915cc0634cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260602} {:answer/id #uuid "919764a7-f044-599d-84f6-09b075397514" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261140} {:answer/id #uuid "97871f23-59b7-5612-bd45-e5666681499e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261190} {:answer/id #uuid "f0dc053c-ee76-590f-8164-11bfcb310e3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261984}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186260330} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e938186-12f9-50c6-849c-59f9dee1509b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "14d76c92-61a7-5867-aa92-05e432da7958" :question/math-academy-id "q-127906" :question/problem "If $M=\\begin{bmatrix}t & 2 \\\\ t & -8\\end{bmatrix}$ is a singular matrix, calculate the value of $t.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $M$ is singular if and only if $det(M)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =t\\cdot (-8)-t\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-8t-2t \\\\  & =-10t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-10t & =0 \\\\ t & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $t$ is $t=0.$"}]}
